    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Look.</strong> Lord of Ravenmoor, 70s. Thin as a rake, velvet robe, raven-headed cane. Dry, dark humor; far more frightened than he lets on.</p><p><strong>Wants.</strong> His new will read at midnight: the manor to Hollow Brook as an orphanage paid for with the moonsilver, as atonement for Elspeth.</p><p><strong><em>Speak with dead</em> (five questions).</strong></p><ul><li><em>Who killed you?</em> “I saw no one. Only the cold. My tonic tasted of mint.”</li><li><em>Was it the ghost?</em> “Elspeth would never harm me.”</li><li><em>Where is the will?</em> “Gone from the box. I heard the bookcase groan before the dark.”</li><li><em>Who knew about the passage?</em> “Hatch. Crane. And the doctor. I showed him myself when my legs failed.”</li><li><em>Anything else?</em> “Under the chapel... silver. Let it build something good.”</li></ul><p><strong>Lines.</strong></p><ul><li>“If I'm dead before the bell, the old will stands, and that I will not allow.”</li><li>“Elspeth walks tonight, they say. She'll have to wait her turn.”</li><li>“It will disappoint everyone at dinner.”</li></ul><p><strong>Note.</strong> Alive only in Act 1. For Act 2, place a second token named 'Lord Silas Ravenmoor (body)' in his study chair with the Dead status.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
